Z||000000||Gokart||04-23-2000||03:54 PM||||Got a K&N today for my GT. We've had alot of rain here lately, when I replaced it there was a puddle of water and the air cleaner that was in there was wet on one side. Makes me wonder if water is getting into the engine when it's raining? I eventually will get Mecham scoops and was thinking about removing that restriction in the plastic box connected to the air cleaner, somebody posted they did this a while back and increased their hp. Maybe that wouldn't be such a good idea unless I stick pipe wrap or a sponge in the scoop on rainy days! Any thoughts?<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 04-23-2000).]||||reg||5
