Z||000005||WKDFIRO||04-24-2000||06:13 AM||||I would think that any good air filter would be able to keep water out of the engine. Now I don't beleive that it won't keep every single little molecule of moisture out but at least keep it from destroying the engine. There are engines that actually have water (A VERY fine mist)injected into the intake for better performance from a turbo. <BR>I would not worry about it. I have driven my 85 GT with a RAM Air scoop (holley kind) through a straight tube, going to the air filter canister through some HEAVY downpours without even a hicup from the engine room. ||||reg||1
